      "stageRecord": "On the ordinary active Form I reading, يكتب is the transitive verb ‘write’, الرسالة is its internal argument, and الطالب is its external argument. External Merge combines the verb with الرسالة; the verb supplies the resulting object's label. الطالب remains a separate workspace object pending introduction of the external argument. The category labels describe Bare Phrase Structure objects, not independently supplied phrase-structure templates. For this analysis, each definite nominal is a lexicalized D object, and the inflected verb is a whole-word terminal; no syntactic decomposition of the article or verbal affixes is posited. The spelling does not display the relevant nominal case endings or the verb's final mood vowel.",
