      "stageRecord": "Merge an active, agent-introducing v with the previously built predicate, and then merge الطالب at its edge. Internal Merge raises the previously displayed V to v, forming a complex head. The lower V occurrence is retained as an unpronounced copy, while the higher occurrence bears the whole-word realization يكتب. This analysis adopts local syntactic head movement, with incorporation preserving the v label. Active v licenses the internal argument's accusative case. The subject remains below the finite head that will subsequently be introduced; consequently, verb–subject order does not require lowering or rightward movement of the subject.",
