      "stageRecord": "Merge a finite T specified for the jussive environment of لم with the v-labeled object. T probes the accessible external argument الطالب, licensing nominative case and singular masculine agreement. This Arabic T has no requirement that an overt subject occupy its edge, so the subject stays in its thematic position. The already formed V–v complex undergoes Internal Merge to T. Its lower occurrence becomes silent, and its higher occurrence pronounces يكتب. The result is the order verb–student–letter. Jussive morphology is treated as a feature of the whole-word verb rather than a separately pronounced suffix; the unvocalized spelling يكتب is compatible with the standard jussive reading يَكْتُبْ.",
