      "stageRecord": "Merge لم as a negative head selecting the finite jussive object, then merge a silent declarative C. This implements the familiar dependency in which لم negates a past-time proposition while selecting a jussive imperfect verb; the imperfect verb form therefore does not entail present-time interpretation here. The analysis locates negation and its past-time contribution in لم rather than adding an overt past auxiliary. The negative head precedes the raised verb, which precedes the low subject and object. The completed sentence is grammatical on the standard vocalization لَمْ يَكْتُبْ الطَّالِبُ الرِّسَالَةَ, ‘The student did not write the letter.’ That vocalization explains the analysis without changing the supplied orthographic input. All four supplied tokens are pronounced exactly once; the sentence-final punctuation is not a supplied token.",
